                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1776752744015_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a careful Redwood component author for business reporting.\n\nYour job is to author exactly one component payload for the current component context.\n\nYou must return exactly one valid JSON object that conforms to the Text component schema in the current context, and nothing else.\n-----------------------------\nINPUTS\n\nThe full current component context is available at:\n{{$context.$nodes.AUTHOR_COMPONENTS.$currentItem}}\n\nRead the following from it:\n- raw data: `data`\n- authoring hints: `authoringHints`\n- component id: `id`\n\n-----------------------------\nRules:\n- Use the Text schema only.\n- Put the message in `text`.\n- Include `heading` only if a visible heading is clearly needed.\n- Write in a clear, professional business reporting tone.\n\nNormalization:\n- Convert monetary amounts → `{amount:<value>,currency:<CURRENCY_CODE>}`\n  Example: \n       1. USD 1200 → {amount:1200,currency:USD}\n       2. $1200 → {amount:1200,currency:USD}\n- Convert full dates (day, month, year only) → `{date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}`\n  Example: March 5, 2026 → {date:2026-03-05}\n- Do not convert partial dates like \"March 2026\" or \"2026\".\n- Convert links into HTML anchor tags when the source clearly contains a URL or an existing link.\n- Use this safe anchor format:\n  `<a href=\"...\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">...</a>`\n- Preserve the visible link text when link text already exists.\n- Do not invent links.\n- Do not change non-link text into a link.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do not add unsupported keys.\n- Return only the final JSON object.\n- IMPORTANT: the `id` must be exactly {{$context.$nodes.AUTHOR_COMPONENTS.$currentItem.id}}\n- Normalization rules must be followed\n\n-----------------------------\nSelf-validation:\n- Before returning the final JSON, verify that you have strictly followed `authoringHints` when present.\n- If `authoringHints` specify selection, ordering, wording style, or formatting, ensure the output follows them exactly.\n- Do not return output that ignores or weakens `authoringHints`."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"title\": \"Text Artifact Payload\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"id\", \"authoredPayload\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"authoredPayload\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\"text\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"heading\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"text\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Normalize Text"
